{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Ox Named Nandivisāla: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja28'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 28 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Kuruṅgavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Four-horned Antelope </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>8. Nandivisālajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Ox Named Nandivisāla: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Manuññameva bhāseyya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One should only speak sweetly, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nāmanuññaṁ kudācanaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>never not sweetly. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Manuññaṁ bhāsamānassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>For the one speaking sweetly, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>garuṁ bhāraṁ udaddhari; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>a large load was pulled, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dhanañca naṁ alābhesi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>earning him money, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tena cattamano ahū”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and he was satisfied with that. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Nandivisālajātakaṁ aṭṭhamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
